# Local run — Bahram + Club + Telegram host

When the user asks to run / boot / start the Bahram site, Club (خانواده), or local Telegram bot, follow this playbook. Do **not** invent ports or deploy polling to production.

## Stack map (Windows / Laragon)

| Piece | Path | Port / URL |
|-------|------|------------|
| Laravel API | `bahram-cm/backend` | `http://127.0.0.1:8010` |
| Next (internal) | via `dev:local` | `:3010` (do not open) |
| سایت بهرام | dual-domain proxy | **http://app.lvh.me:3000** |
| کلاب / خانواده PWA | dual-domain proxy | **http://club.lvh.me:3001** |
| Family Manager (Flutter) | `bahram-family-manager` | **http://localhost:7357** |
| Telegram host app | `telegram/` | **http://127.0.0.1:8088** |
| MySQL | Laragon | `127.0.0.1:3306` — `bahram_backend` + `telegram_host_local` |
| Redis | Laragon | `127.0.0.1:6379` (optional if `QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync`) |

`lvh.me` resolves to `127.0.0.1` — no hosts file edit.

## Boot order (required)

1. Confirm MySQL (and Redis if queue≠sync) is up.
2. Backend: `cd bahram-cm/backend` → `php artisan serve --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8010`
3. Frontend dual-domain: `cd bahram-cm/frontend` → `npm run dev:local` (script: `scripts/dev-local.mjs`)
4. Optional manager: `npm run dev:family` from repo root (or `bahram-family-manager/scripts/run.ps1`)
5. Optional queues: only if `.env` has `QUEUE_CONNECTION=redis` → `php artisan queue:work`
6. Health: `curl http://127.0.0.1:8010/up`, open both lvh.me URLs.

If ports are busy, stop the old listeners first; do not switch to random ports.

## Frontend `.env.local` for dual-domain local

Must match `dev-local.mjs` Host headers:

```
BACKEND_PROXY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8010
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://app.lvh.me:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_DOMAIN=app.lvh.me
NEXT_PUBLIC_FAMILY_DOMAIN=club.lvh.me
```

**Never** leave production `rostami.app` / `rostami.club` as `NEXT_PUBLIC_*_DOMAIN` while running `dev:local` — middleware Host checks will break Club rewrites.

Backend `.env`: `APP_ENV=local`, `FRONTEND_URL` can stay `http://localhost:3000` or list lvh origins in CORS/Sanctum if cookies fail.

## First-time / after pull

```bash
cd bahram-cm/backend
php artisan migrate
php artisan db:seed
php artisan storage:link
php artisan media:sync
```

Admin default (if seeded): `admin@bahram.local` / `password`. OTP local: `OTP_DEV_MODE=true`, code `12345`.

**پنل ادمین (تنظیمات تلگرام، رسانه، …):** `https://rostami.app/admin` — نه `app.lvh.me:3000/admin` (این مسیر وجود ندارد).

## Telegram — preferred: local `telegram/` host app

Prefer running the standalone host (`telegram/`) on this machine over Laravel `telegram:poll`. Iran cannot reach `api.telegram.org` or usually Cloudflare quick tunnels; use the foreign Bot API proxy + local long-poll.

Backend `.env` (Bot API + Iran→host push):

```
TELEGRAM_API_BASE_URL=https://bahram.rahai.online/bahram
PROXY_SHARED_TOKEN=<same as deploy/host-proxy>
TELEGRAM_HOST_PUSH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088/public/host-sync.php
```

One-time / when secrets change:

```bash
mysql -u root -e "CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS telegram_host_local CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;"
cmd /c "mysql -u root telegram_host_local < telegram\db\schema.sql"

php scripts/telegram-local/enable-host.php
```

Every session:

```bash
cd telegram
php -S 127.0.0.1:8088 ../scripts/telegram-local/router.php
# other terminal — only ONE of these (not both, not two local-poll windows):
php ../scripts/telegram-local/local-poll.php
# or from repo root:
# php scripts/telegram-local/local-poll.php
```

Local-only helpers live in `scripts/telegram-local/` — **never upload that folder** (or `config.php`) to the foreign cPanel host.

- Optional: `TELEGRAM_LOCAL_POLL_BOT_TOKEN=` in `backend/.env` + `php scripts/telegram-local/refresh-token.php` so local poll uses a **dev bot** and does not fight production `telegram:reconcile-webhook` every 2 minutes on `@RostamiAppBot`.
- Local Laravel: `TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_RECONCILE=false` so `schedule:work` does not re-register webhook while polling.

- `scripts/telegram-local/router.php` preserves `Authorization` for PHP built-in server (needed by `host-sync.php`).
- `scripts/telegram-local/local-poll.php` deletes the Telegram webhook, long-polls via the proxy, POSTs updates to local `/public/webhook.php`.
- Sync Iran ↔ host uses `127.0.0.1:8010` and `127.0.0.1:8088` on the same PC.
### Fallback — Laravel `telegram:poll` (not host mode)

```bash
cd bahram-cm/backend
php artisan telegram:poll
```

Only when `APP_ENV` is `local`/`testing`. Deletes webhook; ingest goes through Laravel pipeline, not `telegram/`.

### Safety — never break production webhook

- Local poll / `local-poll.php` **deletes** the webhook on that bot token.
- Prefer a **dev/test bot token** in local panel for daily work.
- After testing: restore webhook from admin or `php artisan telegram:webhook:set` on the **Iran server**.
- Never add poll/local-poll to production schedule, deploy, Supervisor/Horizon.

## What AI must not do

- Do not `telegram:webhook:set` pointing localhost/ngrok into production bot without explicit user ask.
- Do not change production `APP_ENV` / deploy polling.
- Do not put site images in `frontend/public/` — follow `site-media-images` rule.
- Do not start only Next without Laravel — Club/admin/API will 502.

